From 146f1336d17812083bc79cef28c6399059873b12 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: TheDBP <TheDBP@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Sun, 13 Sep 2026 10:12:10 -0400
Subject: [PATCH] gapps: drop Velvet (the Google app) from every branch

Velvet is the Google Search app and Assistant. It is the single largest item in the GApps set -- 276
MB on the vic branch -- and the one most likely never to be opened. Dropping it keeps what makes
GApps worth having (Play, Play Services, the app swaps) and removes the part that is mostly bulk.

Nothing useful goes with it. SpeechServicesByGoogle and talkback sit behind the same upstream guard
but are far smaller and cover voice typing and accessibility, so they stay. The -1 feed is already
off via the google-feed-off option, so the launcher side is unaffected. VelvetTitan is behind a
tangorpro-only guard and never applies to any device here.

This was previously a bonito-only patch in that device's repo, justified on space: its retrofit super
left about 42 MB spare and Firefox needs 242 MB. Moving it into the gapps option makes it a property
of the option rather than of one device, so every branch that installs GApps gets the same set.

---
 arm64/arm64-vendor.mk | 1 -
 1 file changed, 1 deletion(-)

diff --git a/arm64/arm64-vendor.mk b/arm64/arm64-vendor.mk
index a91b86c..617705f 100644
--- a/arm64/arm64-vendor.mk
+++ b/arm64/arm64-vendor.mk
@@ -19,7 +19,6 @@ PRODUCT_PACKAGES += \
     MarkupGoogle \
     SpeechServicesByGoogle \
     talkback \
-    Velvet \
     SetupWizard
 endif
 
